# Production Kafka (locked decision)

**Production Streammux** (`kafka_streams` / kstreams1–4, hcvlny) uses **Rednet PNR Kafka** as the sole Kafka cluster for **configuration and management** (the control plane). This is intentional and must not be changed by agents unless the operator explicitly requests it.

## Locked naming (do not change without operator approval)

| Category | Prefix / value |
| -------- | -------------- |
| App/control-plane topics | `net.optimum.experimental.streamlens.streammux.` |
| Job input allowlist (prod) | `net.optimum.`, `com.optimum.`, `gcp.optimum.` |
| Job output allowlist (Rednet data plane) | `net.optimum.` |
| Prod Kafka cluster | Rednet PNR (kb101–kb105 `:9095`, SASL_SSL) |

OneLab may additionally allow `lab.optimum.` for **job input** only; production must not.

## What “configuration and management” means

All Streammux platform services connect to Rednet via `KAFKA_BOOTSTRAP_SERVERS`:

- **job-management-api** — job CRUD, read model, topic allowlists
- **site-orchestrator** — definitions, leases, status, events
- **job-catalog-api** — compacted catalog topic

## App topic prefix (locked — all environments)

All Streammux **app-related** Kafka topics use the prefix:

**`net.optimum.experimental.streamlens.streammux.`**

Canonical names (from `job-contracts` `TopicNames.java`):

- `…jobdefinitions`, `…jobleases`, `…jobstatus`, `…jobevents`, `…jobcommands`, `…jobcatalog`

This prefix applies in **production and OneLab**. Do **not** shorten to `net.optimum.streammux.*` or rename topics without explicit operator approval.

## Job topic allowlists (separate from app topics)

- **Input** — prod allows topics under `net.optimum.`, `com.optimum.`, `gcp.optimum.` only.
- **Output** — prod allows topics under `net.optimum.` (Rednet data plane). Do **not** set output allowlist to the app topic prefix.

Deploy source of truth: `devops/inventory/group_vars/kafka_streams/streammux.yml`.

## Production values (canonical)

| Setting | Value |
| ------- | ----- |
| Cluster | Rednet PNR Kafka |
| Bootstrap | `kb101.srv.hcvlny.alticeusa.net:9095` … `kb105.srv.hcvlny.alticeusa.net:9095` |
| Security | `SASL_SSL`, SCRAM-SHA-512, user `techarch_streammux` |
| App topic prefix | `net.optimum.experimental.streamlens.streammux.` |
| Job input allowlist | `com.optimum.,net.optimum.,gcp.optimum.` |
| Job output allowlist | `net.optimum.` |
| `STREAMMUX_SITE_ID` | `rednet` |

## OneLab differs only on Kafka cluster (not app topics)

OneLab / local dev may use **techarch-kafka** (`*.srv.lab.bthpny.alticeusa.net:9092`, PLAINTEXT) but keeps the **same app topic prefix** above. OneLab input allowlist may include `lab.optimum.`; output allowlist remains `net.optimum.`.

Do **not** copy OneLab Kafka *cluster* settings into production, and do **not** “fix” production by pointing it at techarch-kafka.

## Agent rules

- Do not change `streammux_kafka_bootstrap_servers`, prod SASL settings, app topic names/prefix, or prod allowlists in Ansible unless the operator explicitly asks.
- Do not suggest moving prod Streammux back to `techarch-kapps` or techarch-kafka for the control plane.
- Do not rename app topics to `net.optimum.streammux.*` — that prefix is wrong for this app.
- Do not conflate app topic prefix with job output allowlist — output is `net.optimum.`, not `net.optimum.experimental.streamlens.streammux.`.
- Per-job `streamProperties.bootstrap.servers` in job definitions are separate (job data plane); prod jobs often also use Rednet, but the **platform** cluster above is fixed.
